From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: don't warn about regulatory rules skipped during recovery

During firmware recovery ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list() intentionally
ignores the default regulatory rules the firmware sends after WMI init
("Avoid default reg rule updates sent during FW recovery") by returning
-EINVAL through its retfail label. The caller then logs

  ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to process regulatory info -22

on every successful recovery (seen on both IPQ5018 and QCN6122, with
and without NSS offload). The genuine failure paths in
ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list() already log themselves (the "Failed to
set the requested Country" warning, WARN_ON() in fallback), so drop
the redundant warning while ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY is set.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -7240,7 +7240,13 @@
 
 	ret = ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list(ab, reg_info, IEEE80211_REG_UNSET_AP);
 	if (ret) {
-		ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to process regulatory info %d\n", ret);
+		/* During recovery ath11k_reg_handle_chan_list() deliberately
+		 * rejects the firmware's default rules with -EINVAL when a
+		 * default regd already exists; its real failure paths log
+		 * on their own.
+		 */
+		if (!test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags))
+			ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to process regulatory info %d\n", ret);
 		goto mem_free;
 	}
 
